Package: lpdidcsa
Title: Local Projections DiD and Callaway-Sant'Anna Event Studies
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(person("Olivier", "Godechot", email = "olivier.godechot@sciencespo.fr", role = c("aut", "cre")), person("Ulysse", "Lojkine", role = "aut"))
Description: Implements the local projections difference-in-differences
    (LP-DiD) estimator of Dube, Girardi, Jordà & Taylor (2025) and a
    local-projection version of the Callaway & Sant'Anna (2021)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2020.12.001> estimator (LP-CSA), for absorbing and
    non-absorbing treatments, comparing treated observations with clean
    (never-treated or not-yet-treated) controls at each horizon. Seven
    estimators are available: LP-DiD, which yields a variance-weighted average
    of cohort-specific effects; reweighted LP-DiD and LP-CSA, which yield the
    equally-weighted average treatment effect on the treated (ATT) under
    effects that do not vary with covariates; and LP-DiD with regression
    adjustment, inverse probability weighting LP-DiD and LP-CSA, and doubly
    robust LP-DiD following Sant'Anna & Zhao (2020)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2020.06.003>, which allow effects to vary with
    covariates. Standard errors can account for the estimation of first-stage
    models through cluster-level influence functions. The package also returns
    predicted outcome paths of the treated with and without treatment.
